# Base: consolidated/engine-window-20260926 @ ae3833456 (NOT origin/main, which is 17+ days behind live -- Mayor's 2026-09-21 ruling).
#   Touches internal/config/config.go, internal/config/config_test.go, cmd/gc/cmd_hook_test.go and adds internal/config/work_order_pick_test.go.
#   No overlap with the pending ga-wtzrho / ga-0y849e / ga-1g2if1 patches; ga-473mkh and ga-ljoz23 are already in this base.
# WHAT IT DOES: routed tier 1 (pool probe), tier 2 (gc.run_target migration), tier 3 (ephemeral) and the four assigned leaf queries
#   (in_progress / ready, durable / ephemeral) now hand their survivors to packs/town-deltas/assets/scripts/work-order.sh
#   (ga-9t9acg.1, gate:passed) via `work_order_sort --age reclaim`: priority > type (feature first) > age, with the reclaim
#   anti-starvation clock. Before: tier 1 was `sort_by(.updated_at // .created_at)` over a 20-bead window, the rest took bd's order.
#   - Fetch is `--limit 0` everywhere (filter-then-slice, ga-g7yt): never `--limit=N` before ordering.
#   - The lib runs in a CHILD `bash -c '. "$1" && work_order_sort --age reclaim'`, never sourced into the query's sh: a POSIX-mode sh
#     EXITS when `.` cannot open its file, and dash dies with "Bad substitution" on the lib's bash-only error paths (both reproduced).
#   - Lib absent / unreadable / "cannot tell": `work-order WARN: wo_pick: ...` on stderr, then the SAME survivors through the PREVIOUS
#     order (LRU for tier 1, bd's for the rest). Never empty output, never `2>/dev/null` on the lib's stderr.
#   - Lib lookup: $WORK_ORDER_LIB, else $GC_CITY_PATH, else $GC_CITY (+ packs/town-deltas/assets/scripts/work-order.sh). First one set wins, no cascade.
#   - UNCHANGED on purpose: poolDemandLabelFilterJQ, assignedTierExclusionFilterJQ, moleculeLiveStepFilterShell (the vetoes do not move),
#     the molecule-live-step `--limit 1` existence probe, and the control-dispatcher emit_ready in dispatch_runtime.go.
