#   - gofmt -l on the four files: clean. The Go (including the new test file) is gofmt-clean but was NOT type-checked.
#   - The generated shell, extracted from the Go raw literals, run against a fake `bd` shim, under sh and under /bin/dash, old vs new:
#     P0 feature (newer) vs P0 bug (older); 25 beads with the only P0 feature 25th; reclaimed x2; lib absent; lib erroring in six ways;
#     idle poll; garbage from bd; all three tiers and all four assigned queries. OLD head is the bug / the 20-window; NEW head is the feature.
#   - A Python mirror of work_order_pick_test.go's tables: OLD code 20/104 checks pass, NEW code 118/118, with a mutation control.
#   - work-order.selftest.sh (the lib): see the README.
# Before the swap run (a failure here is a defect of this patch, not of the base: hand the bead back):
#   go vet ./cmd/gc ./internal/config
#   go test ./internal/config ./cmd/gc -run 'WorkOrder|EffectiveWorkQuery|EffectiveAssigned|PoolDemand|RoutedPoolWorkQuery|CmdHook'
